{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PHP",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore, my brethren dearly beloved and longed for, my joy and crown, so stand fast in the Lord, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " dearly beloved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I beseech Euodias, and beseech Syntyche, that they be of the same mind in the Lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I entreat thee also, true yoke-fellow, help those women who labored with me in the gospel, with Clement also, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " other my fellow-laborers, whose names ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the book of life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Rejoice in the Lord always: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " again I say, Rejoice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let your moderation be known to all men. The Lord ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " at hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be anxious for nothing; but in every thing by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known to God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the peace of God, which passeth all understanding, will keep your hearts and minds through Christ Jesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Finally, brethren, whatever things are true, whatever things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " honest, whatever things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " just, whatever things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pure, whatever things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " lovely, whatever things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of good report; if ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " any virtue, and if ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " any praise, think on these things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Those things, which ye have both learned, and received, and heard, and seen in me, do: and the God of peace will be with you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I rejoiced in the Lord greatly, that now at the last your care of me hath flourished again; wherein ye were also careful, but ye lacked opportunity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Not that I speak in respect of want: for I have learned, in whatever state I am, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to be content.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I know both how to be abased, and I know how to abound: every where and in all things I am instructed both to be full and to be hungry, both to abound and to suffer need.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I can do all things through Christ who strengtheneth me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Notwithstanding ye have done well, that ye did communicate with my affliction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now, ye Philippians, know also, that in the beginning of the gospel, when I departed from Macedonia, no church communicated with me as concerning giving and receiving, but ye only.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For even in Thessalonica ye sent once and again to my necessity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Not because I desire a gift: but I desire fruit that may abound to your account.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I have all, and abound: I am full, having received from Epaphroditus the things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which were sent",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from you, an odor of a sweet smell, a sacrifice acceptable, well-pleasing to God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But my God will supply all your need according to his riches in glory by Christ Jesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now to God and our Father ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " glory for ever and ever. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Salute every saint in Christ Jesus. The brethren who are with me greet you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All the saints salute you, chiefly they that are of Cesar's household.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PHP.4.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PHP.4.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with you all. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
